  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "From the graph, we see that\n\n- The slope of the tangent at $x=-4$ is negative, so ${f}^{′}(-4)<0.$\n\n- The slope of the tangent at $x=-2$ is positive, so ${f}^{′}(-2)>0.$\n\n- The slope of the tangent at $x=-1$ is zero, so ${f}^{′}(-1)=0.$\n\nTherefore, ${f}^{′}(-4)<{f}^{′}(-1)<{f}^{′}(-2).$",
